-- title:
--   The `compZero` branch of the p-fibre as a j-line
-- statement:
--   Let $p\ge 5$ be prime and let $\mathfrak X$ be a `DRModelPackage p`, a bundle of data for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the full modular function field of level $p$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$ (properness, flatness, integrality and normality of `DRModel.toBase p`, rational and geometric curve models, sections, a smooth locus, and the further fields of the structure). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, with fraction field $K$ and a ring homomorphism $\iota_K\colon K\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$; write $X$ for the pullback of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb Z\to O$, assumed integral, and let $\varphi\colon X.\mathrm{functionField}\to \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(1\cdot p)$ be a ring homomorphism into the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ obtained from the level-$p$ full modular function field by base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $k$ a perfect, algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, $red\colon A\to k$ a ring homomorphism, $data$ a `ModularPolynomialData p` satisfying the Kronecker congruence $hKr$, $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ the integrality hypotheses for the two degeneracy maps at level $1$ and $p$, $P$ a `PlaceSpecialization A p 1 data hKr k red hα hβ` and $R$ a `ProlongationTuple P`, so that $R.R_1$ is a regular prolongation of $A$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(1\cdot p)$ and $R.\mathrm{residue}_1$ is the associated residue map on $R.R_1.\mathrm{integers}$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,1$, the $k$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k)$ generated by the mod-$p$ $q$-expansion of $j$. Assume $\iota_K(a)\in A$ for every $a\in O$ and that $to\kappa\colon O\to k$ is the composite $a\mapsto red(\iota_K(a))$. Let $\xi$ be the image of the generic point of the underlying scheme of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k$ under $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,k$ followed by $\mathrm{DRModel.baseChangeMap}\,to\kappa$, and impose: (i) $\varphi$ sends the germ at $\xi$ of the global section of $X$ determined by $a\in O$ to the image of $\iota_K(a)$; (ii) $\varphi$ maps every germ in the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,\xi}$ into $R.R_1.\mathrm{integers}$; (iii) germs in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{X,\xi}$ have $R.\mathrm{residue}_1$ equal to $0$; (iv) some germ at $\xi$ is sent by $\varphi$ to $\mathrm{jFun}\,1\,p$, the element of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(1\cdot p)$ given by the $q$-expansion of $j$. Then there is a ring isomorphism $\theta\colon \mathrm{RatFunc}\,k\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,1$ which is the identity on the constants $k$ and which satisfies, for every $u\in\mathcal O_{X,\xi}$, $\theta\bigl((\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k).\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}(\text{image of }u\text{ under the stalk map at the generic point})\bigr)=R.\mathrm{residue}_1(\varphi(u))$.
--
--   This identifies the function field of one labelled branch of the geometric characteristic-$p$ fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(p)$ with the rational function field $k(j)$ over $k$, compatibly with the first residue map of the prolongation tuple; classically it is the statement that this branch is a copy of the $j$-line. It feeds the order comparison in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.nodeResidue_eq_zero_iff_and_ord_eq_of_specializes_of_mem_maximalIdeal_swap`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.nodeResidue_eq_zero_iff_and_ord_eq_of_specializes_of_mem_maximalIdeal_swap).
